-- title:
--   Pullback B'×_B B'≅ B'×_k k[ε] for a principal socle kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative ring, $k$ a field, and $B$, $B'$ commutative rings, equipped with a ring homomorphism $\psi' : O \to B'$, a surjective ring homomorphism $\varphi : B' \to B$ and a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho' : B' \to k$. Suppose $t \in B'$ satisfies $t \neq 0$, $\ker \varphi = (t)$, $t \in \ker \rho'$, and $m t = 0$ for every $m \in \ker\rho'$; let `hfst` be the identity $\mathrm{fst} \circ \iota \circ (\rho' \circ \psi') = \rho' \circ \psi'$, where $\iota : k \to k[\varepsilon] = \mathrm{TrivSqZeroExt}\,k\,k$ is the structural inclusion and $\mathrm{fst} : k[\varepsilon] \to k$ is the first-coordinate homomorphism. Here `pullbackRing` of two homomorphisms into a common target is the subring of the product on which the two composites with the coordinate projections agree, `pullbackFst`/`pullbackSnd` are the two coordinate projections of that subring, and `pullbackStr` is the homomorphism from $O$ induced by a compatible pair of structure maps. The assertion is that there is a ring isomorphism $e$ from $B' \times_B B'$ (the pullback of $\varphi$ with itself) onto $B' \times_k k[\varepsilon]$ (the pullback of $\rho'$ and $\mathrm{fst}$) such that: the first projection of the target composed after $e$ equals the first projection of the source; $e$ carries the structure map of $B'\times_B B'$ given by $(\psi',\psi')$ to the structure map of $B'\times_k k[\varepsilon]$ given by $(\psi',\ \iota\circ\rho'\circ\psi')$; and the second projection of $B'\times_B B'$, precomposed with $e^{-1}$ and with that latter structure map, equals $\psi'$.
--
--   This is the Schlessinger-style comparison of the two pullbacks attached to a small extension whose kernel is generated by a single socle element $t$: the self-fibre-product of $\varphi$ over $B$ is identified with the fibre product of $B'$ with the dual numbers over $k$, compatibly with the first projections and with the $O$-algebra structure maps. It is used in the criterion `bijective_of_isArtinianRing_of_bijective_dualNumber_of_liftsAlong_noetherian_artinLocal_typeFamily`, where bijectivity of a map of deformation functors on Artinian rings is reduced to the case of dual numbers.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormal_ModuliPackage_exists_ringEquiv_pullbackRing_self_dualNumber_of_span_singleton_of_mem.lean

